# VTID-05338 — pipeline-speed/slot-sizing: commands and results
Session kiro-202610220829-5884 (seat exafy), branch kiro/pipeline-speed/slot-sizing, base origin/main 1d5cfda68
(re-checked against origin/main 1478926bb). Windows 11, PowerShell 5.1, Node 24.11.1.

## 1. Installed engine facts (read-only reads of the Kiro agent extension, kiro.kiro-agent/dist/extension.js)
- Watch node schema: {type:"watch", id, handler, config?: record, idleTimeoutSec?: positive number}. idleTimeoutSec
  is a node key (not a config key) and has no upper cap, so the D3a value 86400 is used as planned.
- Idle-timeout behaviour (executeWatch -> completeIdleTimedOutWatch): after idleTimeoutSec of idle polls the watch
  node COMPLETES with payload {"outcome":"idle-timeout"} and watchTerminal=true. In a joinPolicy any gate race that
  means the -skip watch wins after 24 h idle and the work branch is aborted; the race itself ends `completed`, so
  `lanes` (allSettled) does not fail. 24 h is above a 40-iteration slot's wall time (plan D3a); a lane still running
  then is surfaced by the restart watchdog (plan R2) and keeps done:false.
- Command handler config: command (static), pollIntervalSec (min 10), commandTimeoutSec, passthrough for other keys;
  only top-level strings are templated, so the gatedStepIds array reaches stdin unchanged.
- Poll result contract (engine recipe guide, "command handler"): stdout {"outcome":"idle"|"new-activity"|
  "terminal-state","cursor":…,"payload"?}. The key is `outcome` (tasks.md S1 says `status`; the engine wins and
  run-gate.cjs prints `outcome`, like store-review.cjs). Exit 0 with an invalid object fails the node; on Windows
  PowerShell other exit codes arrive as an idle poll, so run-gate.cjs always exits 0.
- Run state: <home>/.kiro/sessions/<dir>/workflows/<wf id>/workflow-state.json; top-level keys workflowId,
  workflowName, status, inputs, artifacts, capturedOutputs, root, createdAt, planRevision, parentSessionId, runLabel,
  originalUserMessages, rootConversationId, workspacePath, …; node statuses pending|running|paused|completed|failed|
  aborted|skipped.

## 2. Status field paths (D3 / R2-F2), from real redacted state files
Scan: node <RUN>/code-1-engine-scan.mjs (138 runs). Observed layout: the tree is `root` → `children`, each node
{nodeId, type, status, iteration?, branchId?, failureReason?, watchTerminal?, children?}; a repeat's children are its
iterations `<repeat id>#<i>` (type sequence, `iteration` set), and the steps inside carry the same `iteration`. There
is no flat `steps[<id>]` map, so the gate looks nodes up by `nodeId` in the tree (every iteration's instance).
- wf_1cf4b73383bba5df (failed inner step in a repeat):
  stage2-spar-loop:repeat:failed > stage2-spar-loop#1:sequence:failed@1 > stage2-round:step:failed@1
  ("Step signaled error via send_message.") — the failure propagates to the iteration and the repeat.
- wf_8e7f53a930509020 (pipeline recipe with the review race):
  lane-slot-6:repeat:failed > lane-slot-6#0:sequence:failed@0 > reviews-6:parallel:failed@0
  ("branch 'rev-6' status=failed") > rev-6/-b/-c:sequence:failed > review-6/-b/-c:step:failed  (all three failed)
  lane-slot-1 > lane-slot-1#0 > reviews-1:parallel:completed > rev-1-b:sequence:aborted (race loser, step completed,
  store watch aborted) — an aborted loser stays in the tree after its race was won.
  lane-slot-2 > reviews-2:parallel (running at the time) > rev-2-c:sequence:failed > review-2-c:step:failed while
  rev-2 / rev-2-b still ran — a tolerated race branch failure.
Consequence (judgement inside the plan, conservative): a gated inner step that is failed/aborted counts as terminal
only if none of the gated steps is running or paused AND no node between it and the gated node is `completed` (an
earlier iteration, a race another branch won) or a still-running `parallel` (a race still going). Without that,
the aborted losers of every won review race would end a healthy lane between the race and land-N. Fixtures in
run-gate.test.mjs: failed-at-repeat, failed-inner-step-in-repeat, failed-inner-step-in-wrapper, failed planning step
(terminal); running, paused, race branch failed while others run, race won with aborted losers before land, earlier
iteration with failed/aborted losers (idle).

## 3. Recipe change
node <RUN>/code-1-transform.mjs .kiro/workflows/vitana-pipeline.workflow.json   (roundtrip check first: equal, LF)
- 11 gate races: investigate-gate, spec-gate, plan-pr-gate, spar-loop-gate, merge-plan-gate
  (parallel any [watch <id>-skip, sequence <id>-work [watch <id>-go, <id>]]) and slot-1..6
  (parallel any [watch slot-N-skip, repeat lane-slot-N with watch slot-N-go first]); every step id kept; review
  races, store watches, land steps and stopWhen unchanged; setup prompt names run.json `plan_pr` and `steps_done`.
- Watch recipe: command `node scripts/collab/run-gate.cjs`, config {run:"{{setup.output}}", role, gatedNodeId,
  gatedStepIds + slot (lane slots), pollIntervalSec:30, commandTimeoutSec:30}, idleTimeoutSec:86400.
- Step nodes 40 (unchanged), max depth 6 (limit 8), 6 lane slots.

